cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Prothon, please cite the method paper below."
title: "Prothon: statistically accurate comparison of protein conformational ensembles"
abstract: >-
  Prothon represents a protein conformational ensemble as a vector of
  probability distributions over local order parameters and quantifies the
  dissimilarity between ensembles by the Jensen-Shannon distance between
  corresponding distributions. The local representation requires no structural
  superposition, so the cost is linear rather than quadratic in ensemble size.
  Every comparison is reported alongside a noise floor measured from disjoint
  halves of each ensemble, which is the smallest difference the available
  sampling can resolve; per-residue significance is assessed against a null
  built by permuting contiguous blocks of conformations, calibrated against
  synthetic systems with known ground truth; and no p-value is reported where
  the data cannot support one.
type: software
license: MIT
